    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d492">

                <pb facs="0660" n="586" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v01/pg586"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 102.1/432</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Sharp</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-12-03T18:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 3, 1917, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2902. For Crosby from McAdoo:</p>
                <p>No. 17. Your No. 11. My own judgment is against two councils. Concentration
                    instead of diffusion is the need of the hour, it seems to me, but am willing to
                    accept your and House’s judgment whatever
                    it may be.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
